//! The `counter-reset` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property creates
//! named [CSS
//! counters](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Counter_styles/Using_counters)
//! and initializes their values. It can create both regular and reversed counters.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: Specifies that no counters are created.
//!
//! Grammar: [ <counter-name> <integer>? | <reversed-counter-name> <integer>? ]+ | none
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-lists-3/#propdef-counter-reset
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/counter-reset
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

